{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולכהן", :translit "u-le-kohen", :gloss "and to/for the priest"} {:he "ולכהן מדין", :translit "u-le-kohen midyan", :gloss "and the priest of Midian"} {:he "לאב ולכהן", :translit "le-av u-le-kohen", :gloss "for a father and for a priest"} {:he "ויהונתן בן גרשום בן מנשה", :translit "vi-honatan ben gershom ben menasheh", :gloss "and Jonathan son of Gershom son of Manasseh"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ולכהן מדין" "לאב ולכהן"]}], :frame {:text "Moses vowed that his firstborn son would serve idolatry, and was punished when that son's own son, Jonathan, became priest to Micah's idol. Jonathan is called בן מנשה (son of Manasseh) but the Nun is suspended, hinting he was truly בן משה (son of Moses); the Sages identify him as Moses' grandson (Bava Batra 109b). The Talmudic principle is that the verse hangs a label of corruption on the one who first enabled it (Bava Batra 109b). Jethro's conversion is described in the Targum to Exodus 18:27, which renders that he was 'circumcised.'", :sources ["Bava Batra 109b" "Targum Jonathan Exodus 18:27"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ולכהן מדין" "לאב ולכהן"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ולכהן מדין", :refs ["Exodus 2:16"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "לאב ולכהן", :refs ["Judges 17:10" "Judges 18:19"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:13:13.653790284Z", :model "glm-5.2"}